 "result": "I documented 8 repos this run: one new backfill and seven updates.\n\nThe backfill was 2026-11-19-orange-drivethru, an app called Lane Listener. It got a new README and CHANGELOG, and its pushed commit landed cleanly. The seven updates were packets, the testbed, itchy-troll and blue-agent, which got new changelog entries and pushes, plus stackloom-meta and hush, which only got release jobs because they already had changelog entries. The mohavetech-website repo only had bot sync commits, so I just refreshed its commit marker. I also refreshed the push times for the repos that only had scribe commits.\n\nThe backfill queue is now empty. The three repos left out are control-troll, heckle-troll and sudosilo, which stay out on purpose.\n\nI pushed the sudosilo profile README and the control-troll state and notes commit. Every repo was reachable.\n\nReleases and repo settings are queued in scribe/publish.json for the scribe-publish workflow to create. I did not check the result of that workflow.\n\nThe shared notes file general.md is now 95 lines, over the 40 line limit. I did not condense it.",
